{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Text-to-Speech (TTS) \u2014 From Tacotron to F5 and Kokoro Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: phonemize input"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from phonemizer import phonemize"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "ph = phonemize(\"Hello world\", language=\"en-us\", backend=\"espeak\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# 'h\u0259lo\u028a w\u025c\u02d0ld'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Phonemes are the universal bridge. Avoid feeding raw text to anything below VITS-level quality."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: run Kokoro (2026 CPU default)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from kokoro import KPipeline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tts = KPipeline(lang_code=\"a\")  # \"a\" = American English"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "audio, sr = tts(\"Please remind me to water the plants at 6 pm.\", voice=\"af_bella\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# audio: float32 tensor, sr=24000"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Runs offline, single file, 82M params."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: run F5-TTS with voice cloning"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from f5_tts.api import F5TTS"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "tts = F5TTS()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "wav = tts.infer("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ref_file=\"my_voice_5s.wav\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ref_text=\"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    gen_text=\"Please remind me to water the plants.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Pass a 5-second reference clip + its transcript; F5 clones prosody and timbre."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: HiFi-GAN vocoder from scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Too big to fit in a tutorial script, but the shape is:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class HiFiGAN(nn.Module):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, mel_channels=80, upsample_rates=[8, 8, 2, 2]):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        super().__init__()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        # 4 upsample blocks, total 256x to go from mel-rate to audio-rate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        ..."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def forward(self, mel):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return self.blocks(mel)  # -> waveform"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Training: adversarial (discriminator on short windows) + mel-spectrogram reconstruction loss + feature-matching loss. Commoditized \u2014 use pretrained checkpoints from `hifi-gan` repo or nvidia-NeMo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: the full pipeline (pseudocode)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "text = \"Please remind me at 6 pm.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "phones = phonemize(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "mel = acoustic_model(phones, speaker=alice)      # [T, 80]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "wav = vocoder(mel)                                # [T * 256]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "soundfile.write(\"out.wav\", wav, 24000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. Builds a phoneme dictionary from a toy vocab, estimates duration per phoneme, and prints a fake \"mel\" schedule.\n2. **Medium.** Install Kokoro, synthesize the same sentence at voice `af_bella` and `am_adam`. Compare audio durations and subjective quality.\n3. **Hard.** Record a 5-second reference clip of yourself. Use F5-TTS to clone it. Report SECS between reference and cloned output."
      ]
    }
